                    <h2 id="divers-GETapi-evaluations-personnel--user_id--score">Task 9: full agent evaluation sheet for a target user over a period.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Endpoint: GET /api/evaluations/personnel/{user}/score</p>
<p>Query params (all optional):</p>
<ul>
<li>start: ISO date Y-m-d. Defaults to today-30 days.</li>
<li>end:   ISO date Y-m-d. Defaults to today.</li>
</ul>
<p>Permission check happens in two layers:</p>
<ol>
<li>Hard role gate: caller must have EVALUATIONS_VIEW_FICHE
in their current workspace (covers manager/cadre/owner/observateur…).</li>
<li>Per-target scope: PermissionService::canViewFicheEvaluation
enforces "own only / cadre→assignees / manager→activity /
owner→workspace" — the actual fiche of $target must be in
the caller's reach.</li>
</ol>
<p>Response shape mirrors EvaluationScoreService::calculerScore() and
adds the target's identity for the UI header.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-evaluations-personnel--user_id--score">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/evaluations/personnel/1/score" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {VOTRE_TOKEN_SANCTUM}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"start\": \"2026-06-04\",
    \"end\": \"2052-06-27\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/evaluations/personnel/1/score"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {VOTRE_TOKEN_SANCTUM}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "start": "2026-06-04",
    "end": "2052-06-27"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "GET",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>


