                    <h2 id="divers-POSTapi-webpush-subscribe">POST /webpush/subscribe</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Persiste une souscription Web Push pour l'utilisateur authentifié.</p>
<p>Comportement « upsert » : si l'endpoint existe déjà pour ce user, on
met à jour les clés et on remet active = true. Cela permet à un
navigateur de re-souscrire après une révocation sans créer de doublon.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-webpush-subscribe">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/webpush/subscribe" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {VOTRE_TOKEN_SANCTUM}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"endpoint\": \"b\",
    \"keys\": {
        \"p256dh\": \"n\",
        \"auth\": \"g\"
    },
    \"content_encoding\": \"aes128gcm\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/webpush/subscribe"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {VOTRE_TOKEN_SANCTUM}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "endpoint": "b",
    "keys": {
        "p256dh": "n",
        "auth": "g"
    },
    "content_encoding": "aes128gcm"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>


<div class="php-example">
    <pre><code class="language-php">$client = new \GuzzleHttp\Client();
$url = 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/webpush/subscribe';
$response = $client-&gt;post(
    $url,
    [
        'headers' =&gt; [
            'Authorization' =&gt; 'Bearer {VOTRE_TOKEN_SANCTUM}',
            'Content-Type' =&gt; 'application/json',
            'Accept' =&gt; 'application/json',
        ],
        'json' =&gt; [
            'endpoint' =&gt; 'b',
            'keys' =&gt; ['p256dh' =&gt; 'n', 'auth' =&gt; 'g'],
            'content_encoding' =&gt; 'aes128gcm',
        ],
    ]
);
$body = $response-&gt;getBody();
print_r(json_decode((string) $body));</code></pre></div>

